Integrity: sha256-9ASD6slTReK0BwLTNxv8ojW9ZSS6WQnZHQ3Pnn+BKI8=
  Re-verify the copy in this tree with:
    openssl dgst -sha256 -binary mathlive.min.mjs | openssl base64

Files here: mathlive.min.mjs, LICENSE, fonts/ (the 20 woff2 files only).

The answer field loads the module at runtime, and only when an answer screen opens:

  const mod = await import('/vendor/mathlive/mathlive.min.mjs');

Why this tree (spec section 4.6):

- The file sits under `public/`, so Vite copies it verbatim into `dist/`. `vite.config.ts`
  marks `/vendor/**` external, so the specifier survives into the bundle as a runtime URL.
  The 841 KB library stays out of the entry chunk. `mathlive` is NOT in `package.json`.
- The deployed CSP is `default-src 'self'` with no `script-src`, no `unsafe-eval`, no
  `worker-src`, and `font-src 'self'` (crates/web/src/security.rs:25-29). Audit of
  `mathlive.min.mjs` on 2026-10-26: zero hits for `eval(`, `new Function`, `new Worker`,
  `new SharedWorker`, `importScripts`. Zero `data:` URIs: the 43 hits of the text `data:`
  are object property names (`{data:e,inputType:"insertText"}`); no hit has a media type
  or `;base64`. `scripts/check-bundle-csp.mjs` runs the same check over `dist/` on every
  build.
- The code sets `MathfieldElement.fontsDirectory` to `/vendor/mathlive/fonts` and
  `soundsDirectory` to null, so the fonts load from the same origin and no sound file loads.
  The sounds directory of the package is not vendored.

To move to another MathLive release, replace the whole directory and redo the audit.

Do not edit these files.
